  "acceptance": "No new product acceptance credit. Four Starport consumer checks remain UNVERIFIED. This API does not connect Starport or qualify native clocks.",
  "contract": [
    "AllowsCatalogAttempt checks the separately accepted consumer authority head against current memory-only permission state. The caller binds the authenticated, validated head to its exact accepted catalog.",
    "An old required revision refuses after withdrawal even when the connected Starmap runtime can serve its replacement. Equal permission revisions permit continued use while a route replacement prepares.",
    "Known publication sequences cannot carry contradictory generation or payload identities. Foreign authorities, policies, future sequences, malformed heads, unknown clocks, expired receipts, and closed runtimes refuse.",
    "Canonical checksum validation preserves lowercase SHA-256 syntax without decoding and re-encoding temporary buffers. Warm valid consumer checks and checksum validation allocate zero times in the regression assertions."
  ],
